hmm, where's 5237? Let me check. Actually doc-055's answer reference_rapport = \"ST-RI-2026-5237\". The text starts with \"RAPPORT D'INTERVENTION ... ANNULE ET REMPLACE ST-RI-2026-4888\". So the current ref must be elsewhere (maybe in a footer \"R\u00e9f. document ST-RI-2026-5237\"). Need care.\n\n6. `date_intervention`: from \"Date of intervention\"/\"Date de passage\"/\"SERVICE DATE\"/\"DATE D'INTERVENTION\" field, or prose (\"The visit took place on 30 November 2025\", \"L'intervention a eu lieu le 18 juin 2025\"). If field \"\u2014\"/\"n.c.\" \u2192 use prose. Note doc-012: DATE D'INTERVENTION \"n.c.\" but answer 2025-05-08 from the \"\u00c9tape/Date\" table (\"Date d'intervention 08.05.25\").\n\n7. `date_validation`: final approval date. From sign-off \"Approved by\" date, or approval stamp image, or prose (\"The report was reviewed on 2 December 2025\" \u2014 but doc-001 answer is 2025-12-03, hmm). Let me re-check doc-001: answer 2025-12-03. Text: \"The report was reviewed on 2 December 2025.\" That's 12-02. Where's 12-03? Maybe the approval stamp image on page 3! Let me check doc-001 images. Yes likely a stamp \"APPROUV\u00c9 ... 03/12/2025\". So date_validation comes from the stamp image, not the \"reviewed\" prose. Important!\n\n8. `volume_dose_ml`: mean of as-left trials (after adjustment). If as-left is \"\u2014\", use prose (\"flow rate as left: 54 mL/min\" for debit; for volume maybe \"On arrival...\" is as-found, not as-left). doc-001: volume_dose 1.05 = \"Delivered volume, mean as left 1.05\". Good.\n\n9. `volume_nominal_ml`: from Nominal volume/Volume nominal/Consigne/Set point field, or diagram image, or prose (\"\u00c0 noter, volume nominal : 25 cm\u00b3\", \"Note, nominal volume: 1 mL\", \"Additional information, nominal volume: 2.5 cl\"). Unit conversions: cl\u219210ml, \u00b5L\u2192/1000, cm\u00b3=ml, L\u21921000ml.\n\n10. `tolerance_ml`: from \"Tolerance\"/\"\u00c9cart maximal tol\u00e9r\u00e9\"/\"Tol\u00e9rance admise\"/\"EMT\"/\"MPE\"/\"Tol\u