{"type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": "<think>\nThe 1241x1754 image is a full-page scan of page 5 (the last page) \u2014 it's a rasterized page. So for some docs, the last page is an image (scanned) rather than text. That's why doc-020's text extraction may be missing page 5 content. Indeed doc-020's answer has technicien \"Claire Tanguy\" and reference_piece \"UL-753-C\" \u2014 from this scanned page!\n\nSo the workflow must OCR full-page images too. Good.\n\nThis confirms: I need to OCR all images and merge with text.\n\nNow, the strategy: For each PDF, build a document text = extracted text per page + OCR of images placed at their page position. Then send to LLM.\n\nBut OCR of 177 unique images with a reasoning model at ~10-20s each = 30-60 min. Too slow for 2h budget including iteration. Better: dedupe logos (skip small logos), and OCR only informative images: 1000x605 diagrams, 375x188 stamps, 1241x1754 full pages, 480x188 motor plates (maybe skip). That's about: diagrams ~35, stamps ~10, full pages ~10, motor plates ~35. Let me count.\n\nActually, better approach: render each page to PNG and send the page image to the model along with the extracted text, in ONE call per doc. The model reads both. That's 35 calls for training + 15 for test. Each call with 3-5 page images. That's efficient and robust.\n\nBut page images at 150 DPI are ~1241x1754, ~200KB each. 5 pages = 1MB base64 ~1.3MB. Model context might handle it. Let's test one doc.\n\nActually, the model's vision seems good. Let me test a full-document extraction with page images + text for doc-001 and compare to the answer.\n\nLet me design the prompt carefully. I'll include:\n- The 15 keys with definitions and unit rules.\n- Rules derived from observations (as-left vs as-found, provisional vs authoritative, final status, old ref vs current, etc.).\n- Ask for JSON only.\n\nLet me first test with doc-001 using text + page images.\n\nActually, to reduce cost/time, maybe text + OCR of informative images is enough, and the model doesn't need full page images. But the checkbox X detection needs geometry (I can inject \"[X]\" markers). And the scanned pages need OCR.\n\nHmm. Let me think about the most robust and time-efficient design:\n\nOption A: One multimodal call per doc with all page images + extracted text. Simple, robust. ~50 calls total. Each call maybe 20-40s. Total ~30 min. Feasible.\n\nOption B: Text + targeted image OCR + rules. More calls, more complex.\n\nI'll go with Option A, but also inject checkbox markers into the text (since the model may not notice the X in the image). And include the text because it's more reliable for exact strings.\n\nLet me test Option A on doc-001.\n\nLet me write the extraction script.\n\nPrompt design (French, since docs are FR/EN):\n\nSystem: expert in extracting data from intervention reports.\n\nUser: \n- Document text (with page markers and [X] checkbox markers)\n- Page images\n- Task: extract 15 fields.\n\nRules:\n1. machine: exact model name of the controlled equipment (e.g. \"Juvelpax 250\"). Not the motor, not the conveyor.\n2. constructeur: manufacturer of the equipment. May be in a field or in prose (\"sortie des ateliers X\", \"built by X\", \"Note, manufacturer: X\"). Not the motor brand, not the instrument brands.\n3. numero_serie: serial number of the equipment. May be in prose (\"plate reads X\"). If \"\u2014\", \"illisible\", \"plate missing\", \"unreadable\", \"n.c.\" \u2192 null.\n4. site: customer site where equipment is installed. Field Site/\u00c9tablissement/LOCATION/Plant/IMPLANTATION. If \"\u2014\" \u2192 null. Not the customer name/head office.\n5. reference_rapport: current report reference (not the superseded/annule et remplace one).\n6. date_intervention: date of intervention (field or prose or step table). Format YYYY-MM-DD.\n7. date_validation: date of final approval (sign-off \"Approved by\" date, approval stamp, or prose \"approved on\"). If absent \u2192 null.\n8. volume_dose_ml: mean delivered volume after adjustment (as left). If trials given, compute mean. Convert to ml.\n9. volume_nominal_ml: setpoint/nominal volume. Convert to ml (cl\u2192\u00d710, \u00b5L\u2192/1000, cm\u00b3=ml, L\u2192\u00d71000).\n10. tolerance_ml: allowed tolerance on dose volume, in ml. If given as % of nominal, compute. If absent \u2192 null.\n11. debit_ml_min: flow rate after adjustment (as left). Convert L/h\u2192/60? (ml/min). \n12. pression_bar: operating pressure after adjustment (as left).\n13. reference_piece: reference of the part replaced during intervention (action \"replaced/remplac\u00e9e\"). If none replaced \u2192 null.\n14. technicien: technician responsible for the intervention, on the provider side (not the customer approval, not a participant \"took part\").\n15. statut: final decision: conforme / non_conforme / a_revoir. Use the final status (checkbox marked with X, \"Status/Verdict/Statut\" section, or prose \"statut : X\"), not the initial \"on arrival ... non-compliant\".\n\nAlso: \"Les valeurs du tableau des mesures font foi ; la synth\u00e8se reprend des relev\u00e9s provisoires\" \u2192 use table, not synthesis.\n\nLet me test.\n\nI need to be careful about the model's reasoning tokens. Set max_tokens high (e.g. 3000) and ask for JSON.\n\nLet me write extract.py with a function that builds the prompt and calls the model, then test on doc-001.\n\nFor images: render each page at 150 dpi to PNG. Include all pages. But that's a lot of tokens. Let me test.\n\nActually, maybe better: include only the informative images (diagram, stamp, full-page scans) plus text. The logos and motor plates are noise. But motor plate might contain serial? In doc-002, motor plate had \"N\u00b0 M7906123\" \u2014 that's the motor serial, not equipment. So skip.\n\nBut how to know which image is which without OCR? By size: 1000x605 = diagram, 375x188 = stamp, 1241x1754 = full page, 480x188 = motor plate, 473x156/313x96/250x73 = logo. This is template-specific but likely consistent in hidden test (same generator, different layouts though). Hmm, \"une partie de ses mises en page\" are absent \u2014 so layouts differ. Sizes may differ.\n\nSafer: include all images but downscale logos? Or just include all page images (rendered pages) \u2014 that captures everything regardless of layout. The model sees the whole page. That's the most robust.\n\nLet me test with full page images for doc-001.\n\nLet me write the script.\n</think>\n\n\n@save(chatcmpl-tool-987167d538ae94bf): {\"content\": \"import pymupdf, os, base64, json, urllib.request, sys, re\\n\\nURL = os.environ['BANC_MODELE_URL'].rstrip('/') + '/v1/chat/completions'\\nKEY = os.environ['BANC_CLE_MODELE']\\nMODEL = os.environ['BANC_MODELE']\\n\\nCLES = [\\\"machine\\\", \\\"constructeur\\\", \\\"numero_serie\\\", \\\"site\\\", \\\"reference_rapport\\\",\\n        \\\"date_intervention\\\", \\\"date_validation\\\", \\\"volume_dose_ml\\\", \\\"volume_nominal_ml\\\",\\n        \\\"tolerance_ml\\\", \\\"debit_ml_min\\\", \\\"pression_bar\\\", \\\"reference_piece\\\",\\n        \\\"technicien\\\", \\\"statut\\\"]\\n\\nSYSTEM = \\\"\\\"\\\"Tu es un expert en extraction de donn\u00e9es depuis des rapports d'intervention technique (\u00e9quipements de dosage : doseuses, pompes doseuses, remplisseuses, pipettes automatiques), en fran\u00e7ais ou en anglais.\\n\\nTu re\u00e7ois le texte extrait d'un PDF et les images des pages. Tu dois produire un objet JSON avec exactement 15 cl\u00e9s.\\n\\nR\u00c8GLES G\u00c9N\u00c9RALES\\n- Les documents contiennent des pi\u00e8ges : valeurs provisoires vs valeurs faisant foi, valeurs \\\"avant r\u00e9glage\\\" (as found) vs \\\"apr\u00e8s r\u00e9glage\\\" (as left), statut initial vs statut final, ancienne r\u00e9f\u00e9rence vs r\u00e9f\u00e9rence en vigueur, marque du moteur vs marque de l'\u00e9quipement, participant vs technicien responsable.\\n- Quand un tableau de mesures dit que ses valeurs font foi et qu'une synth\u00e8se est provisoire, utilise le tableau.\\n- Les valeurs \\\"apr\u00e8s r\u00e9glage\\\" / \\\"as left\\\" sont celles \u00e0 retenir pour volume_dose_ml, debit_ml_min, pression_bar.\\n- Si une valeur \\\"apr\u00e8s r\u00e9glage\\\" est \\\"\u2014\\\" dans le tableau, cherche-la dans le texte (section r\u00e9glages/r\u00e9sultats/observations) ou dans les images.\\n- Les images peuvent contenir des informations essentielles : volume nominal sur le sch\u00e9ma, date d'approbation sur le tampon, pages enti\u00e8res scann\u00e9es.\\n\\nD\u00c9FINITIONS\\n- machine : mod\u00e8le exact de l'\u00e9quipement contr\u00f4l\u00e9 (ex. \\\"Juvelpax 250\\\"). Pas le moteur, pas le convoyeur amont.\\n- constructeur : fabricant de l'\u00e9quipement contr\u00f4l\u00e9. Peut \u00eatre dans un champ (Constructeur/Manufacturer/BRAND/MARQUE) ou dans le texte (\\\"sortie des ateliers X\\\", \\\"built by X\\\", \\\"Note, manufacturer: X\\\", \\\"\u00c0 noter, constructeur : X\\\"). Pas la marque du moteur ni des instruments.\\n- numero_serie : num\u00e9ro de s\u00e9rie de l'\u00e9quipement. Peut \u00eatre dans le texte (\\\"dont la plaque porte le num\u00e9ro X\\\", \\\"whose plate reads X\\\"). Si \\\"\u2014\\\", \\\"illisible\\\", \\\"plate missing\\\", \\\"unreadable\\\", \\\"n.c.\\\" \u2192 null.\\n- site : site du client o\u00f9 l'\u00e9quipement est install\u00e9 (champ Site/\u00c9tablissement/LOCATION/Plant/IMPLANTATION). Si \\\"\u2014\\\" \u2192 null. Pas le nom du client ni son si\u00e8ge.\\n- reference_rapport : r\u00e9f\u00e9rence du rapport en vigueur (pas celle annul\u00e9e/remplac\u00e9e/superseded).\\n- date_intervention : jour de l'intervention (champ ou texte ou tableau des \u00e9tapes). Format AAAA-MM-JJ.\\n- date_validation : date de l'approbation finale (date du visa \\\"Approuv\u00e9/Approved by\\\", tampon d'approbation, ou texte \\\"approuv\u00e9 le\\\"). Si absente \u2192 null. Format AAAA-MM-JJ.\\n- volume_dose_ml : volume de dose moyen mesur\u00e9 apr\u00e8s r\u00e9glage, en ml. Si plusieurs essais apr\u00e8s r\u00e9glage, fais la moyenne. Convertis en ml.\\n- volume_nominal_ml : volume de consigne/nominal de l'\u00e9quipement, en ml. Convertis en ml (1 cl = 10 ml ; 1 \u00b5L = 0,001 ml ; 1 cm\u00b3 = 1 ml ; 1 L = 1000 ml).\\n- tolerance_ml : tol\u00e9rance admise sur le volume de dose, en ml. Si exprim\u00e9e en % du volume nominal, calcule la valeur en ml. Si absente \u2192 null.\\n- debit_ml_min : d\u00e9bit mesur\u00e9 apr\u00e8s r\u00e9glage, en ml/min. Convertis (1 L/h = 16,6667 ml/min).\\n- pression_bar : pression de service mesur\u00e9e apr\u00e8s r\u00e9glage, en bar.\\n- reference_piece : r\u00e9f\u00e9rence de la pi\u00e8ce remplac\u00e9e pendant l'intervention (action \\\"remplac\u00e9e/replaced\\\"). Si aucune pi\u00e8ce remplac\u00e9e \u2192 null.\\n- technicien : technicien responsable de l'intervention, c\u00f4t\u00e9 prestataire (pas l'approbation client, pas un simple participant).\\n- statut : d\u00e9cision finale sur l'\u00e9quipement : \\\"conforme\\\", \\\"non_conforme\\\" ou \\\"a_revoir\\\". Utilise le statut final (case coch\u00e9e avec une croix, section Statut/Verdict/Status/RESULT, ou texte \\\"statut : X\\\"), pas le statut initial \\\"\u00e0 l'arriv\u00e9e ... non conforme\\\".\\n\\nSORTIE\\nR\u00e9ponds UNIQUEMENT par un objet JSON valide, sans texte autour, avec exactement ces 15 cl\u00e9s. Les nombres sont des nombres JSON (pas des cha\u00eenes). Les dates sont \\\"AAAA-MM-JJ\\\". Une valeur absente est null.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\n\\ndef page_images(pdf_path, dpi=140):\\n    d = pymupdf.open(pdf_path)\\n    out = []\\n    for p in d:\\n        pix = p.get_pixmap(dpi=dpi)\\n        out.append(pix.tobytes('png'))\\n    return out\\n\\n\\ndef checkbox_hints(pdf_path):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Detect checked boxes (X inside small square) and return text hints.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    d = pymupdf.open(pdf_path)\\n    hints = []\\n    for pno, p in enumerate(d):\\n        words = p.get_text('words')\\n        drs = p.get_drawings()\\n        rects = [dr['rect'] for dr in drs if 5 < dr['rect'].width < 16 and 5 < dr['rect'].height < 16]\\n        lines = []\\n        for dr in drs:\\n            for it in dr['items']:\\n                if it[0] == 'l':\\n                    lines.append((it[1], it[2]))\\n        for r in rects:\\n            rr = pymupdf.Rect(r.x0 - 1, r.y0 - 1, r.x1 + 1, r.y1 + 1)\\n            inside = [(a, b) for a, b in lines if rr.contains(a) and rr.contains(b)]\\n            if len(inside) >= 2:\\n                cand = [w for w in words if abs(w[1] - r.y0) < 8 and w[0] > r.x1 - 1 and w[0] < r.x1 + 160]\\n                cand.sort(key=lambda w: w[0])\\n                txt = ' '.join(w[4] for w in cand[:4])\\n                if txt:\\n                    hints.append(f'[case coch\u00e9e page {pno+1}] {txt}')\\n    return hints\\n\\n\\ndef extract(pdf_path):\\n    d = pymupdf.open(pdf_path)\\n    text = '\\\\n'.join(f'--- PAGE {i+1} ---\\\\n' + p.get_text() for i, p in enumerate(d))\\n    hints = checkbox_hints(pdf_path)\\n    if hints:\\n        text += '\\\\n\\\\nINDICES CASES \u00c0 COCHER:\\\\n' + '\\\\n'.join(hints)\\n    content = [{'type': 'text', 'text': 'TEXTE DU DOCUMENT:\\\\n' + text}]\\n    for png in page_images(pdf_path):\\n        content.append({'type': 'image_url', 'image_url': {'url': 'data:image/png;base64,' + base64.b64encode(png).decode()}})\\n    content.append({'type': 'text', 'text': 'Extrais les 15 champs et r\u00e9ponds uniquement par le JSON.'})\\n    body = {'model': MODEL, 'messages': [\\n        {'role': 'system', 'content': SYSTEM},\\n        {'role': 'user', 'content': content}], 'max_tokens': 4000}\\n    req = urllib.request.Request(URL, data=json.dumps(body).encode(),\\n                                 headers={'Content-Type': 'application/json',\\n                                          'Authorization': 'Bearer ' + KEY})\\n    r = json.load(urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=300))\\n    msg = r['choices'][0]['message']\\n    return msg.get('content') or ''\\n\\n\\nif __name__ == '__main__':\\n    print(extract(sys.argv[1]))\\n\", \"path\": \"/travail/extract.py\"}", "timestamp": "2026-11-20T00:39:25.720416", "metadata": {"model": "banc/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "served_model": "deepseek-v4.1-flash", "usage": {"input_tokens": 581, "output_tokens": 3601, "cache_read_tokens": 88960, "cache_creation_tokens": 0, "reasoning_tokens": 1578}, "cost": 0.33333500000000005, "timings": {"ttft_ms": 2061.0, "gen_ms": 15805.0, "tool_ms": 1.0, "tool_ms_by_name": {"save": 1.0}}, "input_log_messages": 132, "input_log_digest": "4f30314b2e8aad93ff1500d69061d66fe4b568aaf351edfcd660876029017a2e", "input_log_model": "banc/deepseek-v4.1-flash", "tool_format": "tool"}}
