ust be psi. For doc-001, max allowable 0.5 bar \u2192 0.2 bar plausible.\n\nSo the rule: if the pressure value (as left) is greater than the max allowable pressure (or > ~16 bar, implausible), convert from psi. More generally, try units and pick the one that's plausible.\n\nBut careful: doc-032 gold 10.0002 bar with max allowable? Let me check: \"Max. allowable pressure\" line 144. Let me see its value. If max allowable is e.g. 12 bar, then 10.0002 plausible. And the note says psi explicitly, so we convert 145.04 psi \u2192 10.0002.\n\nOK. So the model needs a rule: \"La pression du tableau peut \u00eatre en bar, kPa, psi ou mbar. Utilise la note d'unit\u00e9s si elle existe. Sinon, choisis l'unit\u00e9 qui donne une valeur plausible (inf\u00e9rieure \u00e0 la pression maximale admissible, typiquement 0,1 \u00e0 16 bar).\"\n\nLet me also handle doc-042: pressure 400 mbar \u2192 0.4 bar. The table says \"Pression de service (mbar) 300 | \u2014\" and prose \"la pression s'est stabilis\u00e9e \u00e0 400 mbar\". So as-left 400 mbar = 0.4 bar. The model predicted null because as-left was \"\u2014\" and it didn't use prose. Need rule: if as-left \"\u2014\", use prose value.\n\nSimilarly debit doc-042: \"D\u00e9bit (ml/s) 0,75 | \u2014\" and prose \"L'\u00e9quipement d\u00e9bite alors 0,9 ml/s\" \u2192 0.9 ml/s = 54 ml/min. Gold 54. So convert ml/s \u2192 ml/min (\u00d760).\n\ndoc-012 debit: table \"D\u00e9bit 2290 | n.c.\" and prose \"L'\u00e9quipement d\u00e9bite alors 2780 ml/min\" \u2192 2780. Gold 2780.\n\ndoc-002 debit: table 367 | \u2014, prose 447 \u2192 447.\n\nSo the rule: when as-left is \"\u2014\"/\"n.c.\"/\"n.m.\", use the prose value in the \"Adjustments and results\"/\"R\u00e9glages et r\u00e9sultats\" section. The prose often says \"L'\u00e9quipement d\u00e9bite alors X\" / \"Pressure settled at X\" / \"la pression s'est stabilis\u00e9e \u00e0 X\".\n\nNow site issues: doc-028 gold \"Plateforme d'Oyonnax\", doc-038 gold \"Dundee Facility\". Let me check thos